<article class="env-lemma" id="0FK1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FK1">Lemma <span data-tag="0FK1">37.62.14</span>.</a> Let $i : X \to Y$ be an immersion. If </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$i$ is perfect, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$Y$ is locally Noetherian, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the conormal sheaf $\mathcal{C}_{X/Y}$ is finite locally free, 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> then $i$ is a regular immersion. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Translated into algebra, this is Divided Power Algebra, Proposition <a href="/tag/0FJS" data-tag="0FJS">23.11.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>